msgid "How to use disposables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:5
#: 4beff7a12c904ed1bc85e93b4af9c025
msgid ""
"A :term:`disposable` is a stateless :term:`qube`, which does not save data "
"between reboots. These qubes can serve various uses cases that require a "
"pristine environment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:7
#: c99988d338de4b14b475506566db6acb
msgid "Viewing untrusted files without other trusted files on the same system;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:8
#: ff5bd12a0f7549c89fafd58bce155327
msgid ""
"Visiting untrusted websites in a web browser without authentication cookies "
"from previous session;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:9
#: cc7a4fad26df4952b3d7002ff7ca88b6
msgid ""
"Sanitizing untrusted PDFs or images and retrieving a safe-to-view image;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:10
#: 48b31a084d8849dc95146da523aefba8
msgid ""
"Connecting untrusted devices in isolation from trusted devices or files;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:11
#: e00e2a50f7d74c749e2577cdec7327b9
msgid "Fresh environment for build systems (for technical users)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:13
#: 5d79108ca7d84460ab9c38a88c2d4cdc
msgid ""
"Disposables can be launched either directly from :term:`GUI domain`'s app "
"menu or terminal window, or from within app qubes. Disposables are generated "
"with names like :samp:`disp{1234}`, where :samp:`{1234}` is a random number. "
"Below is an example of disposable workflow benefits:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:18
#: 77b8856f757d4be19b4eeb8333fc7ef8
msgid ""
"Example of how disposables can be used to safely open untrusted links and "
"attachments in disposables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:20
#: 36bbcaf0f36b4ec4be4af65cb2b95f3d
msgid ""
"In the ``work-email`` qube, the user clicks on a link. This link is opened "
"in a new disposable (through the qrexec protocol :program:`qubes.OpenURL`). "
"The link contains some kind of malware that infects the disposable qube, but "
"it is harmless for the ``work-email`` qube, as the links was opened in a "
"separate environment from the mail client, the mail box is safe. The "
"disposable is later destroyed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:22
#: 5927ec29debf4d4283c4353558201b4d
msgid ""
"In that same *work-email* qube, the user now opens a PDF attachment. Using "
"the qrexec protocol (:program:`qubes.OpenInVM`), the PDF is opened as in a "
"new disposable qube, this time, the file looks clean, but as we can never be "
"sure, the user prefers to default to open files in disposables. The "
"disposable is later destroyed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:24
#: 54ba33496bb64d91b50ce4edfa7b85d8
msgid ""
"This diagram provides a general example of how disposables can be used to "
"safely open untrusted links and attachments in disposables. You may find "
"more on why one would want to use a disposable on the `first disposable qube "
"article <https://blog.invisiblethings.org/2010/06/01/disposable-vms."
"html>`__. Please note that the blog post is dated and some of the "
"information it presents are not accurate anymore."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:27
#: 09cea2777a9f4d82bfde9edfa7c32482
msgid "Disposable types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:31
#: db0739a98a754cfd9ccbbd7aadfb4bbc
msgid "Disposable template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:34
#: f8133b563b45438588c6ad32d5f143e2
msgid ""
":term:`Disposable template <disposable template>` is not a disposable in "
"itself, but a special template that can create different disposable types: "
"normal :term:`disposables <disposable>` and :term:`named disposables <named "
"disposable>`. If you need to have a persistent changes in disposable files "
"(e.g. configuration files), do them in the disposable template. If you need "
"certain programs to be available in the disposable, you can install them in "
"the disposable template's own template. By default, Qubes OS creates the "
"``default-dvm`` disposable template. It will be used it as an example on "
"this page. You can create as many disposable templates as you'd prefer. :doc:"
"`Disposable customization </user/advanced-topics/disposable-customization>` "
"is outside of the scope of this page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:37
#: 018062d519c64bf1ae26e7e1d261a639
msgid "Disposable qube"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:40
#: da68242a61b842efbe38d2d7aca2e025
msgid ""
":term:`Disposables<disposable>` are spawned from disposable templates. They "
"don't have a fixed name and are deleted from the system after the closing of "
"the initial application opened in them. Therefore, *any changes you made in "
"the disposable will be lost*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:42
#: 06e80a49e0af423291edc05c15580872
msgid ""
"For example, you can use the ``default-dvm`` disposable template to create a "
"disposable qube to browse the internet. Every time you launch an application "
"using this disposable template as base, a new disposable qube named :samp:"
"`disp{1234}` (where :samp:`{1234}` is a random number) starts and launches "
"the chosen application. If you close the application window, the :samp:"
"`disp{1234}` qube shuts down and vanishes from your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:44
#: 5fdd1e52a4e64ee28ce1a574071919ec
msgid ""
"Disposables spawned through the Devices widget's **Attach to new in "
"disposable** feature don't have a set initial application - they must be "
"manually turned off when no longer needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:47
#: 4b5da02e946646949f0c88f01972318a
msgid "Named disposable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:50
#: 7ad0ba346e67440591f3a843dbe04c20
msgid ""
":term:`Named disposables<named disposable>` are built upon disposable "
"templates, but they have a fixed name. The named disposable behaves like an "
"ordinary app qube - it doesn't shutdown when you close the initial "
"application, every application you open will start in the same qube, and you "
"need to manually shut it down. However, when it is shutdown, *any changes "
"you made in the named disposable will be lost* - as in any other disposable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:52
#: e40933f6cd0d4a58966a0063afeb039e
msgid ""
"If you have selected during installation to use disposable :term:`service "
"qubes<service qube>`, your ``sys-net``, ``sys-usb`` and ``sys-firewall`` are "
"examples of named disposables based on the ``default-dvm`` disposable "
"template."
msgstr ""

