msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:128
#: 29c21fdb84cd447880f1136aeb7eb079
msgid "Sanitize a file in a disposable (from app qube)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:131
#: e8d0bd26da654cbd8ff251a365f7182a
msgid ""
"There is a nice security property in the system that allows transforming "
"untrusted files into trusted files, this process is called sanitization. A "
"sanitized file, presumably, leaves no room to malicious code, therefore, you "
"can safely open the sanitized file in the qube itself (doesn't need to view "
"in disposable anymore), in a viewer outside of :term:`Qubes OS`, or send the "
"sanitized file to someone that doesn't use :term:`Qubes OS` and can't make "
"the conversion themselves without compromising them.."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:133
#: 1a8ab6fff857425c88439141e305cd86
msgid ""
"Only supported file types for conversions are images and PDFs. The untrusted "
"files will be converted to :abbr:`RGBA bitmap (A raster image where pixels "
"are stored in Red, Green, Blue and Alpha)`. On conversion, the original "
"untrusted files will be moved to :file:`~/QubesUntrustedPDFs` or :file:"
"`image.png-untrusted` (location depends on the file type) while the "
"sanitized file will be created with the same location and name by "
"reconstructing the received data. As the output is an image, the sanitized "
"files are a bit bigger, searching strings without :abbr:`OCR (Optical "
"Character Recognition)` will not be possible anymore."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:135
#: dd128ba327dc4915b32f56d19f2cdc2e
msgid ""
"If you'd like to sanitize a file, in an app qube's file manager, right click "
"on the file (image or PDF) you wish to sanitize in a disposable, then "
"choose :guilabel:`Convert in disposable qube`. Wait a few seconds for the "
"conversion. This conversion runs on its own dedicated qube, a disposable "
"created for the sole purpose of sanitizing this very file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:137
#: 1a1d4b71da494b33bf79491bc6b79979
msgid ""
"It is also possible to do the same on the command line using :program:`qvm-"
"convert-img` and :program:`qvm-convert-pdf`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:140
#: 4759996aa186466e8ff0c70bcea911bc
msgid "Connect a device to a disposable (from GUI domain)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:143
#: d1c3a6cfa7ec4bf59f182e8725ed2d5c
msgid ""
"Sometimes you have a device which you don't trust, therefore you decide to "
"leverage disposables for the task. To attach a device to a disposable, go "
"to :menuselection:`Qubes Devices widget --> <DEVICE> --> Attach to new "
"disposable qube --> default-dvm`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:145
#: 5ad183292d8346fdb88ff7def6561fd2
msgid ""
"No application will launch by default and the disposable will continue "
"running, that is expected, no application request was made. Also notice that "
"opening and closing the first (or any other) application opened in the "
"disposable will not turn it off, this is also expected, you must shutdown "
"disposables created by the Qubes Devices widget manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:148
#: 462ae39be6ae4c35ae99452ef102c3d0
msgid "The same can be done from the command line, although more difficult:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:172
#: 7f9b2a112d304c72873e7993a1f76172
msgid "Faster disposable startup (preloading)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:175
#: 5192111ef5c24feda1d51d147e61bb67
msgid ""
"Disposable qubes can take some time to boot; preloading speeds this process "
"up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:177
#: 82610691bd7f42e0b851f4ee55f1367a
msgid ""
"Preloaded disposables are a type of :term:`disposables <disposable>` started "
"in the background, waiting to be used when needed. They are hidden from most "
"graphical applications by using the :term:`internal <internal qube>` flag. "
"For most intents and purposes, using a preloaded disposable is "
"indistinguishable from using normal disposable qubes, just faster."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:179
#: fd45cc49167d465c8b333dacbdebdf1d
msgid ""
"It is possible to preload from any disposable template as long as it "
"supports :doc:`qrexec </developer/services/qrexec>`, except :term:`Qubes "
"Windows Tools (QWT)` which isn't feature complete yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:182
#: cf5b146f1f1d40fd9317826af7be4734
msgid "Preload disposables from the system's default disposable template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:185
#: b05449ee137140ba8bfdc8bc037302bd
msgid ""
"The system setting applies to whichever disposable template is the system "
"default, so if you change the default, the preloaded disposables will be "
"updated accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:187
#: 551e4982e2d8483292da794c9c681cfd
msgid ""
"Preloading from the system's default disposable is possible with the |qubes-"
"logo-icon|:menuselection:`Qubes App Menu (Q icon) --> Settings (icon) --> "
"Qubes Tools --> Qubes Global Config --> General --> Preload disposable "
"qubes`. You can start with a small number of qubes to preload, for example "
"``2``, and use  :guilabel:`Apply Changes and Close` to save the changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:189
#: e6770d66478044c3ac794fd7f5e34688
msgid ""
"Global config window with preloaded disposables items emphasized and preload "
"disposable setting configured to ``2``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:192
#: dd5e2166f06c4e798ab379afef0eb527
msgid ""
"This can also be changed from the command line from the :term:`GUI domain`, "
"with :program:`qvm-features` targeting ``dom0``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:199
#: 03fef7c5b22842e296df13eba314fa42
msgid "Preload disposables from a specific disposable template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:201
#: 5ff611568f4145f898c7f1a645968fba
msgid ""
"You can also preload disposables from other disposable templates. This can "
"be useful when the disposable template is intended for specific workflows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:203
#: dec7de62d2b4497c94cfd8f2d9faed62
msgid ""
"``default-mgmt-dvm``: :term:`management qube`, used for :doc:`Salt </user/"
"advanced-topics/salt>`, Ansible and Debug Console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:204
#: 7c68191ddab34dea9eb7000bf89f91cf
msgid ""
"``qubes-builder-dvm``: :doc:`Qubes Builder V2 Executor qube </developer/"
"building/qubes-builder-v2>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables.rst:206
#: ca5d62a100234dd885b0857126cf9dd5
msgid ""
"To configure, for example, the ``default-mgmt-dvm`` qube using the app menu "
